        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d5572175-745b-59f7-9e6d-ef0f96578618",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patricia Arquette, Victor Slezak, John Boorman, Tim Robbins, Rhys Ifans, Miranda Otto\n- Films: Beyond Rangoon, True Romance, Ed Wood, Flirting with Disaster, Lost Highway, The Hi-Lo Country, Bringing Out the Dead, Holes, The Bridges of Madison County, The Devil's Own, The Siege, The Cat's Meow, Timequest, The Notorious Bettie Page, Human Nature\n- Places: Burma, Myanmar\n- Events: 8888 Uprising\n\nFacts:\n- Beyond Rangoon is a 1995 drama film directed by John Boorman.\n- Beyond Rangoon is about Laura Bowman, played by Patricia Arquette, an American tourist visiting Burma, now called Myanmar, in 1988 during the 8888 Uprising.\n- Patricia Arquette appeared in the films True Romance (1993) and Ed Wood (1994).\n- Victor Slezak, born July 30, 1957, is an American stage, television, and screen actor.\n- Victor Slezak appeared in The Bridges of Madison County (1995) and Beyond Rangoon (1995).\n- Patricia Arquette appeared in Flirting with Disaster (1996) and Victor Slezak appeared in The Devil's Own (1997).\n- Patricia Arquette appeared in Lost Highway (1997), The Hi-Lo Country (1998), Bringing Out the Dead (1999), and Holes (2003).\n- Victor Slezak appeared in The Siege (1998), The Cat's Meow (2001), Timequest as John F. Kennedy (2002), and The Notorious Bettie Page (2005).\n- Human Nature stars Tim Robbins, Rhys Ifans, Miranda Otto, and Patricia Arquette.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
